WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.500
I want to pick up in September the 6th, 1923 and this is volume 16.

2
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.000
It's speaking about the origin of sin.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Now what Jesus is not doing here is giving a trietize on the fall of Adam or anything else.

4
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:29.000
He's speaking at a particular point to Louisa and he's making a very simple point about people trying to live in the divine will.

5
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.000
How do they slip out of it?

6
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Is that okay?

7
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.000
He's not doing a complete trietize.

8
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Louisa said I felt petrified with pain because of the privation of my sweet Jesus.

9
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.000
It seems to me that even his flashes, his shadow, keep decreasing.

10
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:52.000
My only support is his privation, which like little drops of Jew,

11
00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:00.000
sustained the poor plant of my soul, burned and withered by his privation, giving it a thread of life so as not to let it die.

12
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.000
However, I was all resigned to his will. That's the important thing.

13
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
That's the step one all the time is to be resigned to whatever the Lord allows.

14
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.000
And I tried as much as I could to continue my interior acts.

15
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Now this is volume 16 and we've been told from many volumes that when you go through a period of dryness and prayer and you feel you can't pray, you are to continue as normal.

16
00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Is that okay?

17
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:39.000
So I did as much as I could to continue my interior acts as when I used to take flight together with Jesus in his most holy will.

18
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:49.000
But all how differently I would do them. I would do them badly, not finding everyone so as to give to my God for all.

19
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:59.000
So when you're going through a time of difficulty, it's not easy to do the really fervent prayers because you really need to feel fervent for that.

20
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:09.000
And so you manage to do them but not as well as you would. That's okay. Because in desolation, you know prayer is either consolation or desolation.

21
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Consolation means it's easy for you. Desolation means it's difficult. I'm using the language of the saints here.

22
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:24.000
But consolation and desolation are the normal ebb and flow of prayer.

23
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:34.000
When we're going through a time of consolation and things are easy, then we don't have any problem staying with the prayer and making all kinds of prayers.

24
00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:42.000
If you're going through a period of desolation and you sit beside somebody who's in consolation, you'll actually have to move your seat.

25
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.000
Because the other one will be saying all these prayers of all of this fervor and you can't get a breath out of you.

26
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:57.000
So in order to not get depressed, you'd have to go somewhere where you couldn't see them. I don't know if you understand me. It's actually quite important.

27
00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Now, whether you're in consolation or desolation, it actually doesn't matter. It's just more meritorious if you pray as well, excuse me, if you pray as well as you can in the time of desolation.

28
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:43.000
So, Louisa was saying in her interior, "My Jesus, in your most holy will, I unite my thoughts with yours, and since your thoughts circulate in each creation's intelligence, I want each thought to draw from yours the love of your intelligence in order to place each thought of the creature in the flight of love."

29
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:53.000
Now, she's connecting in the divine will with the intelligence of every person so that that intelligence can be connected to the divine love.

30
00:03:53.000 --> 00:04:09.000
That's our great privilege in the divine will. This flight reaches up on high into heaven before the Supreme Majesty, and blending with the eternal love draws the love of the most holy Trinity upon the earth over all creatures.

31
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:18.000
So, in the divine will, the person has reached up to touch the divine love and to release that divine love upon the earth.

32
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:34.000
Now, while I was doing this and other things, my adorable Jesus moved in my interior and sighing, he told me, "My daughter, you cannot do without me, John 15-5. Without me, you can do nothing."

33
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:45.000
Even less can I be without you, which is the surprise. Okay. Everything you feel in your heart is I. That's what my text says. That's what your text says.

34
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:57.000
We would say is me in English. It's me. Your yearnings, your size, your martyrdom you suffer when you are without me. That's all me.

35
00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:02.000
But the text says it is I, which is not the way we speak in English.

36
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:11.000
It is my heartbeats that reverberate in you, that bring you my pains, and that hide me from you.

37
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:19.000
And this is why when love can endure no more surpassing justice, it forces me to unveil myself.

38
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:33.000
Now, surpassing justice is that you're going into the higher dimension of love operating as distinct from justice operating. Justice is what the creature deserves.

39
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:41.000
And it goes beyond that into the overflow of divine love in us.

40
00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:49.000
Now, this description here is talking about Louisa living in deep union with God.

41
00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:57.000
The problem with all of these writings, and, you know, I shock people if I say to them, I have a problem with Louisa's writings.

42
00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:05.000
In fact, it's a huge problem. And the problem is that in Volume 1, she had three mystical marriages.

43
00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:13.000
Not just one. John of the Cross in the 16th century thought one mystical marriage was the ultimate. Louisa had three.

44
00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:18.000
And the other 35 volumes are sitting on those three mystical marriages.

45
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:26.000
And we who haven't experienced any of the mystical marriages put your hand up if you've had three.

46
00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:43.000
Are trying to see, can we move into this relationship? So we have to understand that the fact that I'm writing on an aircraft does not mean I know how to drive the airplane.

47
00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:56.000
I presume that's perfectly clear to you. Okay, so we are trying to get into the divine will without having this incredible basis that she had.

48
00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:04.000
But even though she had these three spiritual marriages, she still goes through enormous purification.

49
00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:10.000
Therefore, if you and I are not going through purification, there's something wrong.

50
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:22.000
Do you get that? Because if we haven't even reached her level in Volume 1, then we have to go through the purification that gets us to this divine union.

51
00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:33.000
So divine union is 24/7, 365. As Tony Hickey says, you either borrow the divine will or you have it in possession, one or the other.

52
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:45.000
I think most of us are borrowing. Am I right or am I right? So if you're borrowing, you need to understand the process that's actually going on.

53
00:07:45.000 --> 00:08:02.000
So surpassing the justice, he goes on into divine will. You see, if I'm only en route to this experience of divine union, then justice wouldn't want to give me what that divine union will give me.

54
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:14.000
That makes sense. And so he goes beyond that and he actually gives it to you regardless. It's really amazing. And as he was saying this, he made himself seen.

55
00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:21.000
My God, who can say how reborn I felt. She's dying until she sees them and then instantly she's reborn again.

56
00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:34.000
And he said, "My daughter, you gave me the dwelling within you on earth." Now, this indwelling starts with our baptism, the indwelling of the Blessed Trinity in our soul.

57
00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:47.000
It stays with us as we live a life of grace. It grows with our growth in union with God. And it is permanent, absolutely, once you reach union.

58
00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:56.000
In other words, it's with you day and night. You wake up in the night and it's just automatically there. You don't have to get into prayer.

59
00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:04.000
You're in communion all the time. Now, in divine will you get to that place quite quickly. Is that okay?

60
00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:17.000
And I think the Lord air lifts some people into divine will into the union. It's only my opinion that now. It's not a ex-catrede from Rome.

61
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:33.000
"You gave me a dwelling within you on earth and I keep you in heaven inside of my heart." So living in the divine will in this union, you are physically upon the earth, but spiritually you are living the life of the Blessed in heaven.

62
00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:45.000
The divinity delights in the little daughter of the Supreme will, having her in heaven with them. So we have the life of the Blessed before we go to heaven.

63
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:56.000
Now, all the Blessed in heaven would find that if it was possible to be envious there, which it isn't, they would be envious of us because they didn't have this privilege when they were on earth.

64
00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:06.000
And since we have our little daughter in heaven and on earth, it's not worthwhile for us to destroy the earth. That's very interesting.

65
00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:17.000
Now, you have to remember there Genesis 18 and Abraham's intercession for Sodom and Gomorrah.

66
00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:26.000
And the Lord told Abraham in the end that even if there was five decent people, he wouldn't destroy the place.

67
00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:37.000
But of course, there weren't five decent people in Sodom and Gomorrah because Lot and his family living on the edge of that town was benefiting from all the sinful behavior.

68
00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:53.000
So they wanted the world and they wanted God. They'd have fought into a kingdom. So out of respect for Abraham, God rescued Lot and his family, but the wife turned back and her destiny was the same as the others.

69
00:10:53.000 --> 00:11:06.000
So if many of us are living in the divine will, the Lord is going to have more mercy on the earth. This is incredibly important for us to know the effect that we have on our country.

70
00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:10.000
And the effect we have on our world. So let me read it again.

71
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:23.000
Since we have our little daughter in heaven and on earth, it's not worthwhile for us to destroy the earth as justice would want to do and as the creatures deserve.

72
00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:38.000
At most, many cities will disappear. The earth will open chasms at several points, making places and people disappear. Now, I think, and it may be my ignorance, that that hasn't happened yet.

73
00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:42.000
I don't know of whole cities disappearing, do you?

74
00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:53.000
Okay, so therefore you put Amos 3 8 there. Amos 3 8, the Lord tells the prophets ahead of time.

75
00:11:53.000 --> 00:12:06.000
Okay, and very often the saints who are given prophetic messages, some of the messages are for now, some for then and some for way in the distant future.

76
00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:20.000
Wars will decimate the people, but out of regard for our little daughter, we will not destroy the earth, having given to her the task of making our will live on the earth.

77
00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:34.000
Now, somebody has just prodded me, I don't know whether it's Louisa or the Lord, that this is 1923, and if you forward to the Second World War, cities were destroyed.

78
00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:45.000
Dresden was destroyed, and many of the cities of Germany were in fact destroyed. They were attacked by incendiary bombs from the Allies.

79
00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:56.000
Okay, that's why if you're reading this for somebody else, you have to give one ear to your audience and one ear up above, so that you're sensitive.

80
00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:05.000
I didn't get that until I said to you it hasn't happened, and then somebody integrated, it did happen.

81
00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:12.000
Okay, therefore pluck up courage and do not lose heart so much during my absence.

82
00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:23.000
Know that I cannot last too long without making myself seen, I myself cannot do it because he's love and love demands union.

83
00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:32.000
And you never cease to love me, never, not only for yourself, but also for all your brothers.

84
00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:40.000
So I want to give you John 2017 there, the text says all of our dear brothers.

85
00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:46.000
Now, he's just been saying that the earth is so bad, it's fit to be wiped out.

86
00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:58.000
And yet he says to Louisa, I want you to make a reparation for all our dear brothers. I gave you John 2017 because at that text Jesus says to Mary of Magdala,

87
00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:06.000
"Go and tell my brothers that I have risen from the dead." They had all failed him, every one of them, you know what I mean.

88
00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:12.000
And so you see this wonderful love that God has for his creatures.

89
00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:16.000
In fact, do you want to know why Adam sinned?

90
00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:22.000
And this is only for people living at the divine will level, it's not for people living at the worldly level.

91
00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:25.000
It's because he forgot that I loved him.

92
00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:35.000
And what he's looking at there is the very first instance of a slight turning away, the very first act.

93
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:43.000
And he forgot to love me and this was the first seed of his fall.

94
00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:54.000
Take for example, if a temptation comes to me in my mind and I nurse the temptation, then the seed has taken root.

95
00:14:54.000 --> 00:15:05.000
If I reject that first thought to Corinthians 10, 5, you must bring every thought and capture it, put it on to dominion to Christ.

96
00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:15.000
So if every thought is put on to dominion to Christ, then the seed won't take root and there will be no turning away from God and there will be no sin.

97
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:26.000
Is that okay? So this was the first seed of his fall, the fact that he stopped loving and it might only have been in a small way.

98
00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:36.000
Had he thought that I loved him very much and that he was obliged to love me, he would never have decided to disobey me, I think that's very important.

99
00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:45.000
So what the Lord is saying here is that we have to keep remembering that we are loved infinitely, okay?

100
00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:58.000
So I want to give you John 59 as the father has loved me, so I have loved you and that is the way you have to love one another.

101
00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:04.000
So the father loved the son infinitely, absolutely, unconditionally, eternally and that's the way he loves us.

102
00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:10.000
Now as long as we remember that that's the way he loves us, we are going to give a response.

103
00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:18.000
Because the automatic thing inside of us is to respond to love, because love is the essence of our being.

104
00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:34.000
So I want to give you Revelation 2, 5 to 7 as well. Now Revelation 2 from verse 5 is telling the people in Ephesus that they have fallen from their first love.

105
00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:45.000
They are doing good things and he lists the things that are fine that's going on at the place but he said your love is falling and therefore you will fall completely.

106
00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:52.000
So love ceased first and then sin began. That's very interesting.

107
00:16:52.000 --> 00:17:03.000
In other words, if love is the uppermost in our lives, sin hasn't a chance.

108
00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:17.000
And as Adam ceased to love his God, true love towards himself also ceased. Now you can see this to take a graphic example.

109
00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:26.000
If you take people with addictions, what they are doing is showing no love towards themselves because they are actually destroying themselves.

110
00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:35.000
Okay. And notice that if you turn away from love towards any form of sin, you have ceased to love yourself.

111
00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:40.000
And the second commandment is to love your neighbor as yourself.

112
00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:46.000
So if your love for yourself is decreasing, the love for your neighbor is decreasing.

113
00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:59.000
So hence in Genesis chapter 3 you get the fall of Adam and Eve and in Genesis chapter 4 you get the first murder, so the sin against the neighbor.

114
00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:09.000
So Adam's members and powers, now usually the powers are intellect, memory and will, rebelled against him.

115
00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:25.000
He lost dominion, that is dominion over himself. And Jesus has told us in earlier volumes that the only time we truly reign is when we have dominion over ourselves.

116
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:33.000
And then the higher reign is when we hand over that dominion to the divine will, and then the Lord truly reigns in us.

117
00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:39.000
So he lost dominion, he lost order and became fearful.

118
00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:46.000
Now, one of the things that's very important in these writings is the divine order of God, and I want to show you this.

119
00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:53.000
I have other pictures that for me illustrates the divine order of God. I'll pass this around so you can look at it.

120
00:18:53.000 --> 00:19:01.000
Okay. The first thing I want you to see is that everything is perfectly in its place.

121
00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:04.000
If you're meant to be one color, that's the color you are.

122
00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:05.000
Okay.

123
00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:11.000
And the divine order has an absolutely extraordinary beauty. Look at this.

124
00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:14.000
It has an absolutely extraordinary beauty.

125
00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:23.000
And so if I'm meant to be in this ray of light, there's no point in wanting to be in that one. There's no advantage.

126
00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:27.000
So if I'm meant to be in this ray, there's no advantage in wanting to be there.

127
00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:34.000
Not whatsoever, because this ray is as essential to the divine order as any other piece.

128
00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:42.000
So you stop looking at anybody else and your own place, when you let this divine order happen in you,

129
00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:47.000
your place, not only in heaven, but in the universe, is fixed.

130
00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:54.000
And therefore God's divine plan for the whole universe can happen.

131
00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:57.000
So he has to put it into order if you want to look at it.

132
00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.000
I have other pictures if you're interested.

133
00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:03.000
But since I'm on pictures, here's another one.

134
00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:07.000
How would you show a picture of living in the divine will?

135
00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:10.000
I'm eating out of his hands.

136
00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:13.000
He says, "You want to... I'll do it."

137
00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:19.000
Quite literally. And that's also a picture of Isaiah that were carved into the palm of his hands as well.

138
00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:21.000
So you pass that around.

139
00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:25.000
I have other pictures as well because I keep looking for pictures.

140
00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:31.000
Because a picture, to me, says much, much more than a thousand words.

141
00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:36.000
Because once you look at the divine order of God, you'll never try to be in anybody else's place.

142
00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:38.000
Your own place is perfect.

143
00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.000
Does that make sense?

144
00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:47.000
Hence, you've heard me saying for a long time that the Lord does not want us to be carbon copies of each other.

145
00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:49.000
Not at all.

146
00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:53.000
Because if we're all carbon copies of each other, that picture is very boring.

147
00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:56.000
It's all the same color and it's all the same shape.

148
00:20:56.000 --> 00:21:00.000
And he has this infinite variety in the whole thing.

149
00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:07.000
And therefore, he needs an absolutely unique individual response from each one of us.

150
00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:12.000
Therefore, none of us will be responding in the same way as other people are responding.

151
00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:16.000
So we have to be careful not to allow ourselves to become copycats of anything.

152
00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:18.000
Does that make sense?

153
00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:20.000
I hope I've said enough on that now.

154
00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:27.000
It's to allow this divine order to happen inside of us, but also among us.

155
00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:33.000
And when we start letting this divine order operate more and more among us,

156
00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:37.000
what's going to happen is the unique gift of each person is going to come out.

157
00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:41.000
You mightn't even know you have an unique gift, but it'll actually come out

158
00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:46.000
because you'll find yourself that I fit better in this groove than in that one.

159
00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:50.000
And if you operate in the groove that Grace has put you into,

160
00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:54.000
then what God wants to do through you will actually happen.

161
00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:57.000
That's a pre-drum and teen speech, sorry.

162
00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:03.000
So let's come back to this.

163
00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:13.000
So when Adam turned away from love, he lost dominion and order, and he became fearful.

164
00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:21.000
Now he's outside of God's order, and therefore he's outside of God's sense of security.

165
00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:25.000
And the fearful thing is you don't know what to do with yourself,

166
00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:27.000
and you don't know where to place yourself.

167
00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:29.000
You can't be God for yourself.

168
00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:35.000
Now I find it very interesting that shifting away from love, you get into fear.

169
00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:40.000
And St. John says in his first letter, now I can't give you the quotation,

170
00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:43.000
"Perfect love casts out fear."

171
00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:44.000
Okay.

172
00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:55.000
So when you get into the divine union that's in the divine will, fear disappears.

173
00:22:55.000 --> 00:23:00.000
That's one of the signs that you are in that union, is that the fear disappears.

174
00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:03.000
You're not afraid of hell, you're not afraid of purgatory, you're not afraid of death,

175
00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:05.000
you're not afraid of this, that and the other.

176
00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:08.000
And you have people on the earth who are afraid of everything.

177
00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:11.000
They're afraid of their own shadow.

178
00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:21.000
So what the Lord is showing here is someone turning away slowly, initially,

179
00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:25.000
and what they lose in that turning away.

180
00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:29.000
So if fear comes back to us, we have shifted from love,

181
00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:32.000
because perfect love casts out fear.

182
00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:39.000
Not only this, but true love towards other creatures cease as well.

183
00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:45.000
Now true love means your ability to really give to others,

184
00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:50.000
your ability to really see the other person in their own shoes,

185
00:23:50.000 --> 00:23:54.000
and to respond to that person in their own shoes,

186
00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:57.000
that you're not trying to make them a copy of yourself,

187
00:23:57.000 --> 00:24:01.000
you're not trying to control them or dominate them or anything else.

188
00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:09.000
So notice, if you go back two lines, with this ceasing of love,

189
00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:12.000
true love towards yourself disappears,

190
00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:15.000
and therefore true love towards your neighbor disappears.

191
00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:20.000
Now as you watch society outside losing faith in God,

192
00:24:20.000 --> 00:24:23.000
you see fear increasing, violence increasing,

193
00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:27.000
and love of neighbor absolutely disappearing.

194
00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:31.000
Have you noticed? Okay, so it's been described here.

195
00:24:31.000 --> 00:24:36.000
While I created him with the same love, that's divine love,

196
00:24:36.000 --> 00:24:40.000
the same love that reigned among the divine persons,

197
00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:43.000
I created him with divine love,

198
00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:48.000
and so he has descended from an absolutely frightening height,

199
00:24:48.000 --> 00:24:53.000
by which one was to be the image of the other.

200
00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:59.000
So Genesis 1, 27, we were created in the image of God,

201
00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:04.000
Genesis 1, 27, and Romans 8, 29,

202
00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:08.000
we are redeemed into the image of Christ.

203
00:25:08.000 --> 00:25:13.000
That means reordered into the image of Christ.

204
00:25:13.000 --> 00:25:21.000
So this divine love that's poured into us actually makes us the image one of the other.

205
00:25:21.000 --> 00:25:25.000
So if divine love is coming out of us to each other,

206
00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:29.000
it's the surest sign that we are in union with God,

207
00:25:29.000 --> 00:25:33.000
and that God is free to manifest himself.

208
00:25:33.000 --> 00:25:35.000
Because you remember we used to sing it in Latin,

209
00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:38.000
"Ubi carried us at Amor, Deus, Ibi, Est,

210
00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:42.000
where love and kindness is, God is there."

211
00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:45.000
It was one of the lovely things we used to sing.

212
00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:49.000
So I had created him with the same love,

213
00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:52.000
this divine love that reigns among the divine persons,

214
00:25:52.000 --> 00:25:55.000
by which one was to be the image of the other,

215
00:25:55.000 --> 00:26:01.000
one was to be the happiness and the joy and the life of the other.

216
00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:05.000
Now, it was not communicated to me in my childhood

217
00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:09.000
that I was to be the happiness and joy and life of God.

218
00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:12.000
Was it communicated to you? No.

219
00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:14.000
Because they didn't know this stuff.

220
00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:16.000
They didn't understand it at all.

221
00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:20.000
In fact, after the Second World War, there was quite a distorted image of God

222
00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:24.000
as the Punisher, you know.

223
00:26:24.000 --> 00:26:27.000
This is why in coming upon the earth,

224
00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:31.000
the thing on which I placed the greatest important

225
00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:34.000
was that they love one another,

226
00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:38.000
John 13, 34 to 35.

227
00:26:38.000 --> 00:26:42.000
This is my new commandment that you love one another

228
00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:44.000
in the same way as I loved you.

229
00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:49.000
So that means we love one another with divine love.

230
00:26:49.000 --> 00:26:53.000
So again, a pre-dramantine comment.

231
00:26:53.000 --> 00:26:55.000
When we gather in Dramantine,

232
00:26:55.000 --> 00:27:00.000
if we love one another with divine love, miracles will happen.

233
00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:02.000
Is that okay?

234
00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:05.000
But we have to actually consciously love one another.

235
00:27:05.000 --> 00:27:07.000
It doesn't matter whether you like the person or not.

236
00:27:07.000 --> 00:27:09.000
That's a different subject.

237
00:27:09.000 --> 00:27:12.000
It doesn't matter whether you approve of them or anything else,

238
00:27:12.000 --> 00:27:14.000
or whether you see faults or failings in them.

239
00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:18.000
We have to choose to love one another at this divine level,

240
00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:20.000
and then God can work miracles.

241
00:27:20.000 --> 00:27:25.000
I've seen that happen before at a different kind of conference.

242
00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:31.000
So I placed the greatest importance of that they love one another

243
00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:34.000
as they were loved by me.

244
00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:38.000
Now, that's John 15, 9 again.

245
00:27:38.000 --> 00:27:43.000
In order to give them my first love and to let the love of the most

246
00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:46.000
holy trinity hover over the earth.

247
00:27:46.000 --> 00:27:50.000
Now, when love hovers over the earth, there will be life and healing

248
00:27:50.000 --> 00:27:57.000
and growth and reordering back into God's will and growth and everything.

249
00:27:57.000 --> 00:28:00.000
It'll be fantastic.

250
00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:04.000
Therefore, in all of your pains and privations,

251
00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:06.000
never forget that I love you very much.

252
00:28:06.000 --> 00:28:10.000
Now, look at this emphasis that I love you.

253
00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:14.000
That is personal very much.

254
00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:20.000
So as to never forget to love me, that's our response.

255
00:28:20.000 --> 00:28:25.000
And as the daughter of our will, you have the task to love me

256
00:28:25.000 --> 00:28:29.000
for all souls past, present and future.

257
00:28:29.000 --> 00:28:35.000
In this way, you will remain in the order of the divine will you need to add.

258
00:28:35.000 --> 00:28:40.000
And you will fear nothing.

259
00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:43.000
So I think that message is horrendously important.

260
00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:44.000
Is that okay?

261
00:28:44.000 --> 00:28:47.000
I just want to go back over something.

262
00:28:47.000 --> 00:28:50.000
And only when I say it, you'll say yes, okay, okay, okay.

263
00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:54.000
Notice the reason why he wants us to love one another

264
00:28:54.000 --> 00:29:00.000
is that the love of the most holy trinity will hover over the earth.

265
00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:01.000
Okay?

266
00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:06.000
I was told in the book of Genesis chapter 1, page 1,

267
00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:11.000
verse 2, the second verse in the Bible,

268
00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:18.000
that the Spirit of God hovered over what was going to become creation.

269
00:29:18.000 --> 00:29:22.000
And the Spirit of God hovering means that the power of God

270
00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:25.000
is going to bring something incredibly important.

271
00:29:25.000 --> 00:29:30.000
You come to the time of the incarnation that we're jumping a few millennia

272
00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:34.000
and you have the Spirit of God hovering over blessed mother

273
00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:38.000
in order to bring about the miracle of the incarnation.

274
00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:43.000
When you go to the baptism of Jesus, you have the Spirit of God hovering over him

275
00:29:43.000 --> 00:29:49.000
so that he can bring about the whole purpose of redemption.

276
00:29:49.000 --> 00:29:50.000
Fast forward.

277
00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:54.000
When you come to Pentecost, the Spirit of God is hovering over the church

278
00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:58.000
to bring about the miracle of the growth and spread of the church.

279
00:29:58.000 --> 00:30:03.000
Now you fast forward to 2,000 years and the Spirit of God in love

280
00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:06.000
wants to hover over the human race to bring about a new era.

281
00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:08.000
Does that make sense?

282
00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:12.000
I just want to give you a summary of the Bible just in case you've missed it.

283
00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:16.000
And you see, the beautiful thing is he says it in such simple words

284
00:30:16.000 --> 00:30:20.000
that you wouldn't realize he's summarizing the whole thing for you.

285
00:30:20.000 --> 00:30:21.000
Okay.

286
00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:27.000
So to go to a completely different topic, September 9, 1923,

287
00:30:27.000 --> 00:30:30.000
the divine will is hell for Satan.

288
00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:33.000
Very interesting.

289
00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:36.000
What makes hell for him?

290
00:30:36.000 --> 00:30:40.000
So Louisa said, "I still felt some fear that who knows it might not be

291
00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:44.000
my adorable Jesus who dained to speak to me by manifesting to me

292
00:30:44.000 --> 00:30:48.000
so many sublime truths, especially on the divine will."

293
00:30:48.000 --> 00:30:54.000
Now the reason why she has to discern this over and over and over again

294
00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:56.000
is that she's the first person to receive it.

295
00:30:56.000 --> 00:30:59.000
The priests around her don't know what she's talking about.

296
00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:04.000
They have to learn from her what these messages are and where they're going.

297
00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:07.000
So they can't tell her ahead of time.

298
00:31:07.000 --> 00:31:11.000
But they can send her back all the time to discern, discern, discern,

299
00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:13.000
which is very important.

300
00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:20.000
So especially the stuff on the divine will you see that's completely new.

301
00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:24.000
So in case it would be the enemy in order to deceive me.

302
00:31:24.000 --> 00:31:27.000
And while it seems that he flings me up high with so many truths,

303
00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:31.000
he might hurl me down into the abyss in the end, understood.

304
00:31:31.000 --> 00:31:35.000
And I said to myself, "My Jesus free me from the hands of the enemy.

305
00:31:35.000 --> 00:31:39.000
I don't want to know anything all I care about is to save my soul."

306
00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:42.000
Now I laugh when I read that.

307
00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:43.000
Why?

308
00:31:43.000 --> 00:31:47.000
Because she has slipped back below Volume 1.

309
00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:52.000
Volume 1, she was saving her soul before the Lord lifted her up

310
00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:56.000
and you stop looking after yourself and you start looking after his glory

311
00:31:56.000 --> 00:32:00.000
and the salvation of the world and all the rest of it.

312
00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:06.000
But what it illustrates for us is that the moment we get into any little bit of crisis,

313
00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:08.000
we slip back very quickly.

314
00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:11.000
It's just that the Lord is holding her with his two hands

315
00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:13.000
so she's not going to fall anywhere.

316
00:32:13.000 --> 00:32:14.000
Okay?

317
00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:17.000
That's like you taking a small child trying to learn how to walk

318
00:32:17.000 --> 00:32:21.000
and you're holding the two hands so they're not going to hurt themselves.

319
00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:25.000
And blessed Jesus, moving in my interior told me.

320
00:32:25.000 --> 00:32:33.000
Moving in my interior now is Luke 1721.

321
00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:36.000
The kingdom of God is within you.

322
00:32:36.000 --> 00:32:37.000
Okay?

323
00:32:37.000 --> 00:32:41.000
So moving in my interior, Jesus told me, "My daughter, why do you fear?"

324
00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:46.000
Now even at her exalted level, she can still go back into fear.

325
00:32:46.000 --> 00:32:48.000
Now I love when she struggles.

326
00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:52.000
I don't know about you because it consoles me enormously.

327
00:32:52.000 --> 00:32:54.000
And I say, "Lord, when I go through it, it's okay."

328
00:32:54.000 --> 00:32:56.000
She went through it as well.

329
00:32:56.000 --> 00:33:03.000
Don't you know that the thing which the infernal serpent knows the least about is my will?

330
00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:04.000
Why is that?

331
00:33:04.000 --> 00:33:09.000
Because ab eternal, he rebelled against God's will and therefore he knows nothing about it.

332
00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:13.000
In fact, he did not want to do it.

333
00:33:13.000 --> 00:33:16.000
So that's the rebellion of the angels.

334
00:33:16.000 --> 00:33:20.000
And by not doing it, he did not know it.

335
00:33:20.000 --> 00:33:26.000
Now to know it means you don't have the experience and therefore you don't know what to do with it.

336
00:33:26.000 --> 00:33:28.000
Nor did he love it.

337
00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:36.000
So in the divine will, we start off by doing the divine will, getting to know the divine will

338
00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:38.000
and getting to love it.

339
00:33:38.000 --> 00:33:41.000
It's the exact opposite of Satan's experience.

340
00:33:41.000 --> 00:33:48.000
And even less did Satan penetrate the secrets of my inscrutable volition in order to know

341
00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:51.000
the effects and the value of my will.

342
00:33:51.000 --> 00:33:58.000
And if he doesn't know them, how could he speak about it?

343
00:33:58.000 --> 00:34:05.000
Even more, the thing that he abhors the most is that the creature will do my will.

344
00:34:05.000 --> 00:34:11.000
I heard a wonderful story from a person recently, I can't tell you whether they are male or female

345
00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:13.000
or what country or anything else.

346
00:34:13.000 --> 00:34:14.000
Is that okay?

347
00:34:14.000 --> 00:34:16.000
But they were being attacked by Satan.

348
00:34:16.000 --> 00:34:19.000
And Satan was sort of saying, "These are my words now.

349
00:34:19.000 --> 00:34:21.000
There are not anybody else's words.

350
00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:24.000
It's my summary of what I heard."

351
00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:28.000
And Satan was sort of saying, "Who do you think you are?"

352
00:34:28.000 --> 00:34:32.000
She said, "No future for you with the past that you've had."

353
00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:35.000
And the person started listening to the Lord.

354
00:34:35.000 --> 00:34:37.000
"How do I respond to this?"

355
00:34:37.000 --> 00:34:41.000
And started to laugh now with Satan actively attacking.

356
00:34:41.000 --> 00:34:43.000
I said, "Why did you laugh?"

357
00:34:43.000 --> 00:34:49.000
And the person said to me, "The Lord said tell him that his future is worse."

358
00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:59.000
And the person said, "When I told Satan that his future was worse, he disappeared."

359
00:34:59.000 --> 00:35:02.000
It's not interesting, "Who do you think you are?"

360
00:35:02.000 --> 00:35:10.000
You see, a saint is a person with a past and a sinner is a person with a terrible future.

361
00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:14.000
A sinner meaning somebody committed to sin, do you know what I mean?

362
00:35:14.000 --> 00:35:19.000
And so Satan was the sinner with a terrible future.

363
00:35:19.000 --> 00:35:24.000
And the person whom the Lord had redeemed had a past but a wonderful future.

364
00:35:24.000 --> 00:35:29.000
Of course, that's Ezekiel 16.

365
00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:36.000
So how could he know the inscrutable secrets of the divine volition when he's never done it?

366
00:35:36.000 --> 00:35:40.000
In order to know the effects and the value of my will.

367
00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:44.000
And if he does not know them, how could he speak about them even more?

368
00:35:44.000 --> 00:35:49.000
The thing that he abhorsed the most is that the creature will do my will.

369
00:35:49.000 --> 00:35:57.000
The envy of the demons is that we will take their places in heaven, the places they have vacated.

370
00:35:57.000 --> 00:35:59.000
So they'd prefer you not to have it.

371
00:35:59.000 --> 00:36:06.000
He doesn't care about whether the soul, watch this now and put a big envy about two feet high.

372
00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:14.000
He doesn't care about whether the soul prays, goes to confession, receives communion, does penance and even works miracles.

373
00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:19.000
But the thing that harms him the most is that the person will do my will.

374
00:36:19.000 --> 00:36:21.000
And that's extremely important.

375
00:36:21.000 --> 00:36:31.000
I couldn't underline it enough because if you go back into the approximately volume eight to ten,

376
00:36:31.000 --> 00:36:37.000
Louisa was struggling with the fact that she was no longer suffering the crucifixion and all of this,

377
00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:39.000
and she thought she was being completely useless.

378
00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:42.000
And the Lord said to her, "Look, it's not the suffering.

379
00:36:42.000 --> 00:36:44.000
Suffering in itself is not it.

380
00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:48.000
It's whether I want you to do it.

381
00:36:48.000 --> 00:36:51.000
So it's suffering in my will.

382
00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:56.000
And if my will doesn't want you to suffer, it's my will that's important."

383
00:36:56.000 --> 00:37:00.000
So the Lord does different things with us.

384
00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:09.000
In fact, as Satan rebelled against my will, so was hell created.

385
00:37:09.000 --> 00:37:13.000
I want you to note the next two words and ring them.

386
00:37:13.000 --> 00:37:15.000
You may never have realized it before.

387
00:37:15.000 --> 00:37:18.000
It was created in him.

388
00:37:18.000 --> 00:37:21.000
Now that is actually correct.

389
00:37:21.000 --> 00:37:32.000
Because when people go through a terrible time, supposing a family breakup, and they also tell,

390
00:37:32.000 --> 00:37:36.000
what they're saying is they are hellishly unhappy.

391
00:37:36.000 --> 00:37:40.000
And that's correct. The hell is inside of you.

392
00:37:40.000 --> 00:37:48.000
And when a person is taken out of that situation and brought into grace and into holiness,

393
00:37:48.000 --> 00:37:54.000
then they experience heaven, meaning you're going towards love more and more and more.

394
00:37:54.000 --> 00:38:00.000
So hell is the absence of love, and heaven is the presence of love. God is love.

395
00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:07.000
So hell was created in him. His unhappy state, the rage that consumes him.

396
00:38:07.000 --> 00:38:09.000
Isn't that interesting?

397
00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:17.000
So my will is hell for him, and every time he sees a soul who is submitted to my will,

398
00:38:17.000 --> 00:38:22.000
knowing its qualities, value, and sanctity, he feels his hell being doubled.

399
00:38:22.000 --> 00:38:25.000
Now that's only a manner of speech. The hell isn't doubled.

400
00:38:25.000 --> 00:38:28.000
In other words, he feels it all the more.

401
00:38:28.000 --> 00:38:37.000
Because he sees the paradise, the happiness, and the peace that he lost being created in the soul.

402
00:38:37.000 --> 00:38:38.000
That's fantastic.

403
00:38:38.000 --> 00:38:44.000
So I want to give you Ezekiel 16 to read as a background to this.

404
00:38:44.000 --> 00:38:52.000
Because there you're told that the person who was a sinner and who turns to the Lord,

405
00:38:52.000 --> 00:38:57.000
that everything of the past is just wiped away, and the Lord only looks at where you're going.

406
00:38:57.000 --> 00:38:59.000
That he doesn't look at your past.

407
00:38:59.000 --> 00:39:06.000
But then, but if someone who was good then turns to evil, all the good in your past is forgotten.

408
00:39:06.000 --> 00:39:10.000
And where you're going, which is down to hell, is what he looks at.

409
00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:13.000
And it looks awfully unjust on the second side.

410
00:39:13.000 --> 00:39:18.000
Because we think that because we did some good in the past, we should be let off the hook.

411
00:39:18.000 --> 00:39:21.000
And he says, "No justice is the same on both sides."

412
00:39:21.000 --> 00:39:30.000
And the more my will is known, this is the whole reason for studying all of this material,

413
00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:34.000
the more tormented and furious he becomes.

414
00:39:34.000 --> 00:39:42.000
So if you never get any kickback from him, get worried and ask a bit of advice, will you?

415
00:39:42.000 --> 00:39:48.000
So how can he possibly speak to you about my will if it forms his hell?

416
00:39:48.000 --> 00:39:56.000
And if he did speak to you, his words would form hell in you because you can only give what you have.

417
00:39:56.000 --> 00:40:01.000
Because he knows my will only to hate it, not to love it.

418
00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:05.000
And what is hated never brings happiness and peace.

419
00:40:05.000 --> 00:40:17.000
But behind all of this, I think the Lord is saying to us to look at the way that people who have walked away from God

420
00:40:17.000 --> 00:40:26.000
and are feeling so disturbed in conscience about it, don't want to look, don't want to repent how they will lash back at the believer.

421
00:40:26.000 --> 00:40:31.000
The hell in them cannot tolerate the heaven in you.

422
00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:33.000
Does that make sense?

423
00:40:33.000 --> 00:40:38.000
So just understand it as a reason for persecution.

424
00:40:38.000 --> 00:40:49.000
And besides, Satan's word is empty of grace, therefore he cannot confer grace to do my will.

425
00:40:49.000 --> 00:40:53.000
You'll never grow in holiness by listening to Satan.

426
00:40:53.000 --> 00:40:58.000
You just tell him to get lost and tell him that his future is pretty rough.

427
00:40:58.000 --> 00:41:03.000
So let's come to September the 14th, 1923.

428
00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:11.000
And the purpose for which man was created was for him to always revolve around God.

429
00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:13.000
Now look at it.

430
00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:18.000
You've been given the essence of the message there as the earth revolves around the sun.

431
00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:22.000
Now the earth continuously revolves around the sun.

432
00:41:22.000 --> 00:41:23.000
It never stops.

433
00:41:23.000 --> 00:41:26.000
And if it stops, it will disintegrate.

434
00:41:26.000 --> 00:41:27.000
Okay?

435
00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:32.000
So Louisa said, I was thinking of how all things revolve around the sun.

436
00:41:32.000 --> 00:41:37.000
The earth ourselves, all creatures, the sea, plants everyone.

437
00:41:37.000 --> 00:41:40.000
We all revolve around the sun.

438
00:41:40.000 --> 00:41:44.000
It's a funny statement she's making there because we don't do it separately.

439
00:41:44.000 --> 00:41:50.000
It's the earth that revolves around the sun and that gravity is holding you to the earth.

440
00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:53.000
So whatever the earth does, you do.

441
00:41:53.000 --> 00:42:00.000
And because we revolve around the sun, we are illuminated and we receive a seat.

442
00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:10.000
So the sun reflects its burning rays upon all and we, the whole of creation by revolving around the sun,

443
00:42:10.000 --> 00:42:15.000
enjoy its light and receive part of the effects and good which the sun contains.

444
00:42:15.000 --> 00:42:18.000
Now notice part, you can't receive it all.

445
00:42:18.000 --> 00:42:20.000
Not actually possible.

446
00:42:20.000 --> 00:42:34.000
Now how many things do not revolve around the divine sun, although the angels, the saints, men and all created things, even our queen mother.

447
00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:39.000
Does she perhaps not hold the first round in which rapidly revolving around the divine will?

448
00:42:39.000 --> 00:42:43.000
She absorbs all the reflections of the eternal sun.

449
00:42:43.000 --> 00:42:54.000
Now, while I was thinking about this, my divine Jesus moved in my interior and clasping me all to himself, he told me, my daughter,

450
00:42:54.000 --> 00:42:59.000
this was precisely the purpose for which I created man.

451
00:42:59.000 --> 00:43:06.000
Try telling that to somebody who doesn't know the divine will writings and they'll think you've lost it, won't they?

452
00:43:06.000 --> 00:43:10.000
That you were created to revolve around the sun.

453
00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:13.000
Let's say, where did you go to school?

454
00:43:13.000 --> 00:43:22.000
My daughter, this was precisely the purpose for which I created man, that he would always revolve around me.

455
00:43:22.000 --> 00:43:28.000
And I like the sun, why around the Lord? Because he's the source of our lives, the source of absolutely everything.

456
00:43:28.000 --> 00:43:36.000
And I like the sun, being at the center of the round would reflect in him my light, my love, my lightness and all my happiness.

457
00:43:36.000 --> 00:43:42.000
In other words, the sun is the source of life on earth, so the Lord is the source of our life.

458
00:43:42.000 --> 00:43:51.000
At each round of his, I would give him every new contentment's beauty and arrows more burning.

459
00:43:51.000 --> 00:43:57.000
Now, the more burning arrows coming from the Lord, what do you think it is? It's love.

460
00:43:57.000 --> 00:44:06.000
And when you do the hours of the Passion, you hear Louisa describing the burning love that was inside of him.

461
00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:12.000
Before man sinned, my divinity was not hidden to man. Isn't that interesting?

462
00:44:12.000 --> 00:44:22.000
Because by revolving around me, he was my reflection, and therefore he was the little light.

463
00:44:22.000 --> 00:44:31.000
So it was as though natural that I, being the great sun, the little light would be able to receive the reflections of my light.

464
00:44:31.000 --> 00:44:39.000
But as soon as he sinned, he stopped revolving around me. That's where the disintegration begins.

465
00:44:39.000 --> 00:44:47.000
We've lost the divine order and were not in our correct place in the whole order of things.

466
00:44:47.000 --> 00:44:53.000
He stopped revolving around me. His little light became dark.

467
00:44:53.000 --> 00:45:08.000
Now, beside that, I want to give you Matthew 6, verses 22 to 23, where Jesus said, "If your light is darkness, how very dark it's going to be in your interior."

468
00:45:08.000 --> 00:45:18.000
So his little light became dark. He became blind, and he lost the light to be able to see my divinity in his mortal flesh.

469
00:45:18.000 --> 00:45:29.000
As much as a creature is capable of. So much so that in coming to redeem man, I took on mortal flesh in order to let myself be seen.

470
00:45:29.000 --> 00:45:40.000
Now, notice we could only see flesh. We have moved so far from being spiritual beings that we can now only see material things.

471
00:45:40.000 --> 00:45:48.000
That tells you how much we have deteriorated as a race. So I took on mortal flesh in order to let myself be seen.

472
00:45:48.000 --> 00:45:57.000
Not only because man had sinned with the flesh, and with the flesh I was to expiate, but because he lacked the eyes to be able to see my divinity.

473
00:45:57.000 --> 00:46:09.000
Now, you get back the eyes through contemplation. Is that okay? Contemplation and adoration of the Eucharist, you get back the eyes.

474
00:46:09.000 --> 00:46:24.000
This is so true that my divinity, which dwelled in my humanity, that's Colossians 2, 19, all the divinity dwelled in the humanity of Jesus. Colossians 2, 19.

475
00:46:24.000 --> 00:46:33.000
That my divinity, which dwelled in my humanity, could only unleash through glimpses and flashes a few rays of light from my divinity.

476
00:46:33.000 --> 00:46:44.000
Now, while Jesus was on earth, those few rays were the night he showed his apostles that he walked on water. They saw him walking on water.

477
00:46:44.000 --> 00:46:50.000
The day they saw him transfigured on Mount Table. That was during his lifetime.

478
00:46:50.000 --> 00:47:03.000
Then after the resurrection, when they had been purified enormously, then they were able to see him in his resurrection, and they were able to see him in his ascension.

479
00:47:03.000 --> 00:47:10.000
Tremendous gift for the church. So see then what great evil sin is.

480
00:47:10.000 --> 00:47:25.000
It is for man to lose his round around his creator, to annul the purpose of his creation, to be transmuted from light into darkness, from beautiful into ugly.

481
00:47:25.000 --> 00:47:43.000
It is such a great evil that with all of my redemption, I could not restore to him the eyes to be able to see my divinity and his mortal flight. Why is that?

482
00:47:43.000 --> 00:48:06.000
To be purified sufficiently to be able to see. But the saints have seen at least momentarily. So I could not restore to him the eyes to be able to see my divinity and his mortal flight, but only when this flash undone and pulverized by death could rise again on the day of judgment.

483
00:48:06.000 --> 00:48:14.000
So the whole of humanity is only going to see him again on the day of judgment. Sad, isn't it?

484
00:48:14.000 --> 00:48:21.000
What would happen if the whole of creation could fall short of its revolution around the sun?

485
00:48:21.000 --> 00:48:30.000
All things would be upset. They would lose light because they get light from the sun. They would lose harmony. They would lose beauty.

486
00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:45.000
Each would bump into each other. In other words, you'd have chaos. And even if the sun were present, because they would not be revolving around it, the sun would be as though dead for the whole of creation.

487
00:48:45.000 --> 00:49:04.000
In other words, not able to give its life giving fruits at all. Now, because of original sin, man lost his round around his creator and therefore he lost the order and the dominion of himself, he lost the light.

488
00:49:04.000 --> 00:49:18.000
Now, since the beginning of the church, saints have referred to growing in holiness as "enlightenment" that you receive more and more light.

489
00:49:18.000 --> 00:49:39.000
In other words, that your interior receives more and more light. When you go into the higher volumes of Louisa, that is the over 20s. You'll find that Louisa becomes more and more light and therefore she's able to describe the divine will more and more clearly.

490
00:49:39.000 --> 00:49:51.000
And I love the passages where she says, "This is an endless light. There's no way out. It's just like Alice in Wonderland. You know what I mean?" Having arrived in this place.

491
00:49:51.000 --> 00:50:07.000
And Jesus says to her, "There is no way out. You are permanently here. In other words, you are having heaven now. The only difference is that on earth you still suffer because the body has to go through its things."

492
00:50:07.000 --> 00:50:16.000
So every time a human being sins, not only does he not revolve around his God, but he makes his stops around the goods of redemption.

493
00:50:16.000 --> 00:50:29.000
You're not even picking up the helps that Jesus has made available for us in redemption, which, like a new son, came to bring him forgiveness, escape and salvation.

494
00:50:29.000 --> 00:50:39.000
But do you know who it is that never stops around her son? It is the soul who does my will and lives in it.

495
00:50:39.000 --> 00:50:52.000
She always runs. She never stops. She receives all the reflections of my humanity and also the reflections of the flashes of my divinity as well.

496
00:50:52.000 --> 00:50:57.000
So I'm going to stop there for tonight.
